From 11be4cccac45b0205b9d176861cc1fd9861a3ee7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 08:58:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): exclude every implementer model from review
 routing [daveey]

Review routing previously inferred authorship only from a concrete card pin.
Unpinned and downstream reviews could retain class:deep, while the pacing
governor bypassed review-peer exclusion and selected the author again.
Collect concrete non-review run models (result before route), author pins,
and downstream creator/child provenance. Resolve known-author reviews to
independent concrete routes and preserve mandatory reviewer pins. Filter
pace/wall reroutes and fail closed on an unsafe pace offer; record the full
implementer set and concrete handoff model in routing receipts.

Proof: regression on main 9f236d888bed: 15 passed, 36 failed; fixed: 51 passed.
Three mutants killed via sdlc-review/scripts/mutants.py: governor exclusion,
paced_route exclusion and base resolver exclusion. Full 42-file consumer
suite passes; scripts/check --base origin/main passes. Read-only copy of
replica, seven incident review runs in recorded lanes with current worker
registry/pools: MATCH none-on-implementer 7/7. Replay uses snapshot author
provenance, not historical pool reconstruction. Exact-head independent
review, required CI and post-deploy proof remain landing gates.
